        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kele Okereke, Jon Hume\n- Bands: Bloc Party, Evermore\n- Music releases: \"What Did I Do?\", \"The Hunter\"\n- Roles: lead singer, rhythm guitarist\n\nFacts:\n- Kele Okereke was born on 13 October 1981.\n- Jon Hume was born on 6 November 1983.\n- Kele Okereke is a British musician also known by the mononym Kele.\n- Kele Okereke is best known as the lead singer and rhythm guitarist of the indie rock band Bloc Party.\n- Jon Hume is the lead singer of the New Zealand band Evermore.\n- Jon Hume is the eldest of the three brothers who make up Evermore.\n- \"What Did I Do?\" is a song by Kele Okereke.\n- \"What Did I Do?\" was released as the first single from Kele Okereke's EP \"The Hunter\".",
